;; EXPECT: ok
;; TYPES: machine
;; Regrouped views of a set (design 07 §7.5, "Regrouped views"; Lean
;; `regroup_idem_overlap_lost`, `RegroupLaws.lean`). Regrouping replaces the group by its class:
;; with sab = S{A, B}, the view {A, B, C} regroups to {C, sab}. By idempotence S{A, B, C} also
;; equals S{A, C, sab} and S{B, C, sab}, sets over classes present, but no regrouping keeps a
;; member of the group beside its class, so (S x y z) never binds x = sab, y = A, z = C while
;; (S x y) binds x = sab, y = C. With `(set-option :completion eager)` s equals S{sab, A, C}.
(sort E)
(function A () E) (function B () E) (function C () E)
(function S (E) E :assoc-comm-idem)
(function U2 (E E) E)
(function U3 (E E E) E)
(let sab (S (A) (B)))
(let s (S (A) (B) (C)))
(rewrite (S x y) (U2 x y) :flatten)
(rewrite (S x y z) (U3 x y z) :flatten)
(run 2)
(check-eq s (U2 sab (C)))
(check-neq s (U3 sab (A) (C)))
